\subsection{Formatting question groups}

A question group renders as a heading stating the draw---how many of the
pool's questions each student gets and at what points---followed by the pool
questions formatted as usual.  The function returns the next question number
along with the markdown, so the caller can continue numbering the questions
after the group.

<<functions>>=
def format_classic_question_group(entry, start_number):
  """Formats a question group entry as markdown.

  Args:
    entry: Group entry {"group": {...}, "questions": [...]}
    start_number: Number for the first pool question

  Returns:
    Tuple of (markdown string, next question number)
  """
  group = entry.get('group', {})
  pool = entry.get('questions', [])

  lines = []
  <<format the group heading>>

  number = start_number
  for question in pool:
    lines.append(format_classic_question(question, number))
    lines.append("")
    number += 1

  return "\n".join(lines), number
