Canvas accepts a [[pick_count]] larger than the pool without complaint;
students then get fewer questions (and points) than intended.  An empty pool
is likewise legal---the group just never yields any questions---but almost
certainly a mistake in the JSON.  Both cases are silent on the server side,
so we warn client-side.

<<warn about suspicious pool sizes>>=
pick_count = clean_spec.get('pick_count')
if not pool:
  canvaslms.cli.warn(f"question group '{name}' has an empty question pool")
elif pick_count and pick_count > len(pool):
  canvaslms.cli.warn(
    f"question group '{name}' picks {pick_count} questions "
    f"but its pool only has {len(pool)}")
